From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:05:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: integrate T8132 IOMFB as a common DCP backend

Keep display components, atomic state and framebuffer ownership in appledrm
while adding the qualified IOMFB 26.6 wire backend. Snapshot bounded
callback inputs and retain uncertain scanout until exact successor
receipts.

Generated-by: Codex
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
[ryan: rebased onto 7.3 integration/aurora; the linear-only modifier
list is format_modifiers_no_ix there]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
[dylan: Kconfig: DRM_APPLE_DCP_T8132 added next to omacom's
 DRM_APPLE_DCP_T6030_AUDIO. dcp_backlight.c: kept omacom's
 dcp_backlight_presents_nits() and the v14.7 panel-nits paths and ORed in
 iomfb_is_m4(), matching the resolution on integration/aurora.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
